  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342261",
      "title": "Using the Oak Framework with Deno",
      "lectureOrder": 527,
      "videoOrder": 468,
      "sourceHash": "470c78011c921a2e0d3028a6146947a4c061e6b9ea53c03942b745f27db9ec25",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.8,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "Now, throughout this course you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 8.71,
          "en": "how you can process requests with Node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.71,
          "end": 11.56,
          "en": "And you saw that it isn't too much fun",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.56,
          "end": 16.5,
          "en": "if you do this all on your own without any extra framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.5,
          "end": 18.17,
          "en": "The code that you have to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.17,
          "end": 20.68,
          "en": "could look something like this, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.68,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "Now this is Node code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 25.33,
          "en": "But in Deno, or Denos world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.33,
          "end": 27.76,
          "en": "it would be pretty much the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.76,
          "end": 31,
          "en": "Out of the box, if you just used the core APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31,
          "end": 33.57,
          "en": "but also if you used the standard library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.57,
          "end": 36.2,
          "en": "you would have to do all the requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.2,
          "end": 39.7,
          "en": "processing and the response, body handling and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.7,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "You would have to do all of that on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 45.19,
          "en": "You would have to pass incoming request bodies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.19,
          "end": 48.84,
          "en": "And whilst it's nice to see what happens under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 51.44,
          "en": "I will not repeat it here because it's really not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.44,
          "end": 55.27,
          "en": "that different from what you learned about Node there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.27,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "Instead, the main takeaway, just as in Nodes case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "is that we typically don't want to do this on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 68.12,
          "en": "Instead, we want to do this with help of some frameworks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.12,
          "end": 71,
          "en": "which take care of the heavy lifting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71,
          "end": 75.03,
          "en": "which take care of the request body processing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.03,
          "end": 78.76,
          "en": "and which allow us as a developer to focus on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.76,
          "end": 80.75,
          "en": "our core business logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.75,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "And that, by the way, will be true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 86.48,
          "en": "no matter which kind of web application we plan on building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.48,
          "end": 89.21000000000001,
          "en": "We can, of course, build two main kinds of web apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.21000000000001,
          "end": 92.02000000000001,
          "en": "and that would be APIs and server-side rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.02000000000001,
          "end": 94.09,
          "en": "views based web apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.09,
          "end": 98.13,
          "en": "So, for example, REST API or GraphQL API apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 100.17,
          "en": "where you have those endpoints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 102.31,
          "en": "where you then have a standalone frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.31,
          "end": 104.53,
          "en": "that communicates with the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.53,
          "end": 106.94,
          "en": "Or the other use case that you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.94,
          "end": 110.74000000000001,
          "en": "server-side rendered views with templating engines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.74000000000001,
          "end": 114.28,
          "en": "and you generate HTML on the server and send that back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.28,
          "end": 116.96000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore you have one frontend, backend unit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.96000000000001,
          "end": 119.25,
          "en": "This is what you learned about in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 121.89,
          "en": "You had a look at teamplating engines in that course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.89,
          "end": 123.8,
          "en": "We also learned about REST APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.8,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "And you can use Deno for all kinds of apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 130.76,
          "en": "Just like you can use Node for all kinds of apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.76,
          "end": 134.6,
          "en": "You can also render server-side templates with Deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.6,
          "end": 137.68,
          "en": "and then you can also build APIs with Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.68,
          "end": 140.4,
          "en": "In this module I will focus on APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.4,
          "end": 144.15,
          "en": "Simply that's a bit easier and allows me to focus more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.15,
          "end": 148.3,
          "en": "on Deno and not on overhead-like templating engines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.3,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "But in the end, you can build everything with Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "That's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 155.15,
          "en": "No matter what you're building though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.15,
          "end": 158.82999999999998,
          "en": "as I mentioned, you don't wanna do all that request passing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.82999999999998,
          "end": 160.6,
          "en": "and so on, on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.6,
          "end": 164.63,
          "en": "So let's now see which frameworks we have with Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.63,
          "end": 167.23,
          "en": "and how they would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.23,
          "end": 171.64,
          "en": "In Node.js, we have the Express framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.64,
          "end": 173.72,
          "en": "We learned about Express in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.72,
          "end": 178.18,
          "en": "and Express is a great and very popular Node framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.18,
          "end": 180.64,
          "en": "that takes care of the heavy lifting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.64,
          "end": 183.2,
          "en": "and allows us, as developer, to focus on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.2,
          "end": 184.853,
          "en": "our core business logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.77,
          "end": 190.77,
          "en": "In Deno, or Denos case, we have the Oak framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.85,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "Just like Express, it's a middleware focused Deno framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 200.22,
          "en": "So learning Oak will be easy if you already know Express",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.22,
          "end": 202.56,
          "en": "for building web applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.56,
          "end": 205.81,
          "en": "Now, it's actually not directly inspired by Express,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.81,
          "end": 209.17000000000002,
          "en": "but by Koa, which is another framework that exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.17000000000002,
          "end": 213.51,
          "en": "for Node.js which I haven't covered in this course though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "Now if you search for Koa, you'll find koajs.com.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 220.52,
          "en": "And there you'll learn that it's a next generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.52,
          "end": 223.27,
          "en": "web framework for Node.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.27,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "In the end you could say that Koa basically has the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 229.27,
          "en": "of being a better Express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.27,
          "end": 231.79,
          "en": "If you have a look at some code examples here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.79,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "you'll see that it's also middleware based.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 237.38,
          "en": "It's not too far away from express,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.38,
          "end": 240.56,
          "en": "but it does some things differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.56,
          "end": 243.01,
          "en": "You can check out Koa for Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.01,
          "end": 245.47,
          "en": "if you wanna learn all about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.47,
          "end": 248.84,
          "en": "But in general, Express still is the most popular framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.84,
          "end": 252.2,
          "en": "and Koa was inspired by Express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.2,
          "end": 257.2,
          "en": "Now, Oak, on the other hand is a Deno third party module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.02,
          "end": 260.74,
          "en": "And you'll find it under third party modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.74,
          "end": 262.69,
          "en": "on the Deno page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.69,
          "end": 265.26,
          "en": "And here you find a lot of modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.26,
          "end": 267.76,
          "en": "that can help you with a lot of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.76,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "But if you search for Oak, you'll find that Oak module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.68,
          "end": 276.14,
          "en": "And that's, again, just this Koa,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.14,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "and therefore indirectly Express inspired framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 281.96,
          "en": "for Deno now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.96,
          "end": 285.61,
          "en": "You also just make that clear if you search for Express,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.61,
          "end": 290.61,
          "en": "find certain frameworks that are basically Express for Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.3,
          "end": 295.01,
          "en": "Those frameworks might be powerful in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.01,
          "end": 297.58,
          "en": "but at the moment a lot of features are missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.58,
          "end": 301.35,
          "en": "in those frameworks which is why I'm not covering them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.35,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "That's why we will stick to Oak for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 308.06,
          "en": "Just as with Node and so on, there simply are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.06,
          "end": 310.05,
          "en": "different frameworks available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.05,
          "end": 312.58,
          "en": "different libraries available which you can look into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 312.58,
          "end": 314.5,
          "en": "to solve different problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 314.5,
          "end": 316.95,
          "en": "The main problem which they tried to solve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316.95,
          "end": 318.55,
          "en": "is always the same though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.55,
          "end": 321.42,
          "en": "They want to make it easier for you to write your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 323.56,
          "en": "and they want to take annoying work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 323.56,
          "end": 326.92,
          "en": "like passing request bodies away from you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 326.92,
          "end": 329.31,
          "en": "So if we dive into that Oak module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.31,
          "end": 332.4,
          "en": "we get some documentation there on how we use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 335.40999999999997,
          "en": "And we can follow this basic code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.40999999999997,
          "end": 338.48,
          "en": "we can implement this basic code snippet here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 338.48,
          "end": 342.53,
          "en": "to handle incoming requests, and send back responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.53,
          "end": 345,
          "en": "with the Oak module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345,
          "end": 348.39,
          "en": "Now, the most important difference to note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.39,
          "end": 353.39,
          "en": "at this point here, is that we have no package.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 353.88,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "and that we don't have a tool like NPM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 359.29,
          "en": "for managing dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 359.29,
          "end": 363.68,
          "en": "With Express, we had core modules, which we had to import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 363.68,
          "end": 366.62,
          "en": "But which were installed together with Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 366.62,
          "end": 370.01,
          "en": "And we had third party modules, like Express,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 370.01,
          "end": 373.29,
          "en": "which we had to install with NPM Install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 373.29,
          "end": 375.54,
          "en": "Right, that's what we did over and over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 375.54,
          "end": 376.8,
          "en": "throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 376.8,
          "end": 380.87,
          "en": "We had to manage dependencies for our project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.87,
          "end": 383.77,
          "en": "With Deno, this concept does not exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.77,
          "end": 388.62,
          "en": "Because there, with Deno, you have these URL imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.62,
          "end": 391.25,
          "en": "So you never install anything locally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 391.25,
          "end": 395.28,
          "en": "you never manage local dependencies like this with Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.28,
          "end": 399.47,
          "en": "Instead with Deno you really just reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.47,
          "end": 402.68,
          "en": "to a web server, to a file on that server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 402.68,
          "end": 405.43,
          "en": "and you can install it from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 405.43,
          "end": 407.6,
          "en": "Now, you can still manage some versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.6,
          "end": 411.46,
          "en": "by including them in the URL from which you're importing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 411.46,
          "end": 414.61,
          "en": "but you don't have a dedicated package management file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
